# Paranal Airglow Line And Continuum Emission (PALACE) model: data and code of
# v1.0 (Noll et al. 2024)
# 
# Illustration of the calculation of the PALACE reference intensities for O
# recombination lines as listed in pmd_reflineint_atom.dat
# 
# Column names:
# lam: vacuum wavelength in µm (NIST)
# ID: 12 characters describing upper and lower states (NIST)
#     (see pmd_reflineint_atom.dat for details)
# Ei: energy of upper state in 1/cm (NIST)
# Aij: Einstein-A coefficient in 1/s (NIST)
# gi: statistical weight (NIST)
# wmp: weight of multiplet component (based on Aij and gi)
# rc: radiative recombination coefficient in cm3/s for optically thin case and
#     a temperature of 1,000 K (escalante+92)
# reffeat: reference feature measured in X-shooter data
#          (see pmd_intdata_atom.dat):
#          OI0777 for quintet and OI0845 for triplet upper states
# Iref: reference intensity in R for reffeat (see pmd_intdata_atom.dat)
# rI: intensity of line relative to Iref (based on wmp and rc)
# I: reference intensity in R (based on Iref and rI)
# 
# References:
# escalante+92: https://doi.org/10.1016/0032-0633(92)90127-A
# NIST: https://physics.nist.gov/asd
# 
